ef", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 17553, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01AWnVcWLeuaxbhzw6bzepZb", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18, all regions on v2.3.1). Per the runbook, I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy (v2.2.9 was older). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed (us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1). I retried the rollback to v2.3.0, which completed in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: investigate why v2.3.1 failed health checks, and investigate the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback attempt. v2.3.1 should not be redeployed until it is fixed and verified in staging."}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 48153, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01AWnVcWLeuaxbhzw6bzepZb", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 48153, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01AWnVcWLeuaxbhzw6bzepZb", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49192, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RaR39rCrXsKcuPtN2dwGqE", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 49492, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RaR39rCrXsKcuPtN2dwGqE", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_ac